From d32186ada90cce82b5f346bfcdfcb841d518b027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Takle <aadiatakle@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:34:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(exam): ?debug=1 convergence dock, and back-to-back
 bursts within a fast type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The debug dock renders the ability estimate CONVERGING while the test is taken:
the pooled estimate, the plausible range around it, that range per reasoning
area on a shared 1..20 axis, and the range's width after every answered item so
the narrowing is visible rather than inferred. Built as a pure function of the
answered-item trace, so the panel is a view of the session rather than a second
copy of it, and the running estimate it prints is recomputed with the engine's
own `difficultyDelta` and the scorer's own `deriveAbilityFit` — no second
implementation of ability.

Bursts serve several items of one type back-to-back so an instruction is read
once. Not a fixed mini-set: `update` has already moved the area estimate, so
`nextItem` re-targets and the burst adapts to the earlier answers. Which types
qualify is derived from item structure (a bounded unpaced choice, no process
measurement), not a hand-picked list; length steps down one item per option
above four, so the wired banks run 6/5/4.

The runner's debug gate moves to `?debug=1` with `?telemetry=1` kept as an
alias. The `?telemetry=1` on the demo iframe URL is D-028's separate ratified
contract and is untouched. Gating stays URL-only exactly as before.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
